  "story": "Two hikers each wrote down the numbers of the peaks they climbed, in order; a hiker may climb the same peak more than once. They want the longest list of peaks that both climbed in the same order: peaks may be skipped in either diary, but the order may not change. How long is that list? With diaries 3 1 2 and 1 2 3 the answer is 2 (peak 1, then peak 2).",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "first", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "second", "type": "array<num>"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 0, "max": 60},
    "notes": ["Each diary lists 0 to 60 peaks.", "Peak numbers are whole numbers from 1 to 30."]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.add", "arith.max", "arith.sub", "arr.append", "arr.get", "arr.len", "arr.set", "cmp.eq", "cmp.lt", "cmp.ne", "ctrl.else", "ctrl.for_range", "ctrl.foreach", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "ctrl.while", "lit.num", "logic.and", "new.array", "var.get", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 93
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 600000, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 20000},
  "hints": ["Answer a smaller question for every pair of beginnings: the longest shared list using only the first i peaks of one diary and the first j peaks of the other.", "If peak i and peak j are EQUAL, the answer is one more than the answer for the two shorter beginnings. If not, it is the MAX of the answers with peak i dropped or with peak j dropped.", "Keep these answers row by row, each row a NEW LIST: one row per peak of the first diary, one entry per beginning of the second, starting with 0. A row only needs the row before it."],
  "validators": {"output": "equal"},
